  "question": {
    "text": "A coil has resistance 30 ohm and inductive reactance 20 ohm at $50 \\mathrm{~Hz}$ frequency. If an ac source, of 200 volt, $100 \\mathrm{~Hz},$ is connected across the coil, the current in the coil will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ZCXxi",
      "text": "$4.0 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "w4lq2",
      "text": "$8.0 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "7tSUh",
      "text": "$7.2 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "pfkBo",
      "text": "$2.0 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "If $\\omega=50 \\times 2 \\pi$ then $\\omega \\mathrm{L}=20 \\Omega$ If $\\omega^{\\prime}=100 \\times 2 \\pi$ then $\\omega^{\\prime} \\mathrm{L}=40 \\Omega$\nCurrent flowing in the coil is\n$$\n\\mathrm{I}=\\frac{200}{\\mathrm{Z}}=\\frac{200}{\\sqrt{\\mathrm{R}^{2}+\\left(\\omega^{\\prime} \\mathrm{L}\\right)^{2}}}=4 \\mathrm{~A}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
